{"id":"8cd200016e351244","group":"58","path":"58/batch08/58-thm-hellinger.md","title":"Hellinger–Toeplitz Theorem","display":"thm-hellinger — Hellinger–Toeplitz Theorem","type":"theorem","metadata":{"type":"theorem","book":"Set Theory","book_abbrev":"58","label":"58-thm-hellinger","aliases":["58-thm-hellinger"],"display":"thm-hellinger — Hellinger–Toeplitz Theorem","depends_on":["[[../batch13/58-df-hilbert-space.md]]","[[../batch07/58-df-linear-operator.md]]","[[../batch03/58-df-bounded-operator.md]]","[[../batch15/58-df-self-adjoint.md]]"]},"metadataError":null,"renderWarnings":[],"properties":[{"key":"type","html":"theorem"},{"key":"book","html":"Set Theory"},{"key":"book_abbrev","html":"58"},{"key":"label","html":"58-thm-hellinger"},{"key":"aliases","html":"<div class=\"property-array\"><span>58-thm-hellinger</span></div>"},{"key":"display","html":"thm-hellinger — Hellinger–Toeplitz Theorem"},{"key":"depends_on","html":"<div class=\"property-array\"><span><a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-1\" data-note=\"b70ce791d5b1a19b\" href=\"?note=b70ce791d5b1a19b\" title=\"../batch13/58-df-hilbert-space.md\">../batch13/58-df-hilbert-space.md</a></span><span><a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-2\" data-note=\"9fa59a08139e4466\" href=\"?note=9fa59a08139e4466\" title=\"../batch07/58-df-linear-operator.md\">../batch07/58-df-linear-operator.md</a></span><span><a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-3\" data-note=\"2ad9c248fe18df37\" href=\"?note=2ad9c248fe18df37\" title=\"../batch03/58-df-bounded-operator.md\">../batch03/58-df-bounded-operator.md</a></span><span><a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-4\" data-note=\"5998e080b5d378a0\" href=\"?note=5998e080b5d378a0\" title=\"../batch15/58-df-self-adjoint.md\">../batch15/58-df-self-adjoint.md</a></span></div>"}],"html":"\n<h2 id=\"Hypothesis\">[Hypothesis]</h2>\n<ul>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"H,T,\\langle\\cdot,\\cdot\\rangle\\in V\">\\(H,T,\\langle\\cdot,\\cdot\\rangle\\in V\\)</span> and <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\mathbb K\\in\\{\\mathbb R,\\mathbb C\\}\">\\(\\mathbb K\\in\\{\\mathbb R,\\mathbb C\\}\\)</span></li>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"T\\in H^H\">\\(T\\in H^H\\)</span> (everywhere-defined operator)</li>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{HilbertSpace}_S:V^2\\to\\{\\top,\\bot\\}\">\\(\\mathrm{HilbertSpace}_S:V^2\\to\\{\\top,\\bot\\}\\)</span> and <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{Linear}_{\\mathbb K}(-;H,H)\">\\(\\mathrm{Linear}_{\\mathbb K}(-;H,H)\\)</span></li>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{BoundedOperator}_S:V^3\\to\\{\\top,\\bot\\}\">\\(\\mathrm{BoundedOperator}_S:V^3\\to\\{\\top,\\bot\\}\\)</span> and <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\operatorname{SelfAdjoint}_S:V^2\\to\\{\\top,\\bot\\}\">\\(\\operatorname{SelfAdjoint}_S:V^2\\to\\{\\top,\\bot\\}\\)</span></li>\n</ul>\n<h2 id=\"Assertion\">[Assertion]</h2>\n<figure class=\"equation\" data-tex=\"\\begin{aligned}\n\\mathrm{thm\\text{-}hellinger}\\vdash&amp;\n\\mathrm{HilbertSpace}_S(H,\\langle\\cdot,\\cdot\\rangle)\n\\land T\\in H^H\n\\land\\mathrm{Linear}_{\\mathbb K}(T;H,H)\\\\\n&amp;\\land\n\\forall x,y\\in H\\;\n\\bigl(\n\\langle T(x),y\\rangle=\\langle x,T(y)\\rangle\n\\bigr)\\\\\n&amp;\\to\n\\mathrm{BoundedOperator}_S(T,H,H)\n\\land\\operatorname{SelfAdjoint}_S(T,H).\n\\end{aligned}\"><div class=\"math-display\" tabindex=\"0\" role=\"region\" aria-label=\"数学公式\">\\[\\begin{aligned}\n\\mathrm{thm\\text{-}hellinger}\\vdash&amp;\n\\mathrm{HilbertSpace}_S(H,\\langle\\cdot,\\cdot\\rangle)\n\\land T\\in H^H\n\\land\\mathrm{Linear}_{\\mathbb K}(T;H,H)\\\\\n&amp;\\land\n\\forall x,y\\in H\\;\n\\bigl(\n\\langle T(x),y\\rangle=\\langle x,T(y)\\rangle\n\\bigr)\\\\\n&amp;\\to\n\\mathrm{BoundedOperator}_S(T,H,H)\n\\land\\operatorname{SelfAdjoint}_S(T,H).\n\\end{aligned}\\]</div><button class=\"equation-action\" type=\"button\" aria-label=\"展开查看完整公式\">展开公式 ↗</button></figure><h2 id=\"Remark\">[Remark]</h2>\n<ul>\n<li>Hellinger–Toeplitz says that an everywhere-defined symmetric operator is automatically bounded; bounded symmetry then gives self-adjointness.</li>\n<li>Unbounded symmetric operators may fail to be self-adjoint.</li>\n<li>The linearity predicate now matches the scalar-field-parameterized operator definition used upstream.</li>\n</ul>\n","headings":[{"id":"Hypothesis","text":"[Hypothesis]","level":2},{"id":"Assertion","text":"[Assertion]","level":2},{"id":"Remark","text":"[Remark]","level":2}],"links":[{"target":"../batch13/58-df-hilbert-space.md","status":"resolved","id":"b70ce791d5b1a19b","anchor":"ref-1","targetAnchor":"","location":"元数据 · depends_on","heading":"","excerpt":"[[../batch13/58-df-hilbert-space.md]]","embed":false},{"target":"../batch07/58-df-linear-operator.md","status":"resolved","id":"9fa59a08139e4466","anchor":"ref-2","targetAnchor":"","location":"元数据 · depends_on","heading":"","excerpt":"[[../batch07/58-df-linear-operator.md]]","embed":false},{"target":"../batch03/58-df-bounded-operator.md","status":"resolved","id":"2ad9c248fe18df37","anchor":"ref-3","targetAnchor":"","location":"元数据 · depends_on","heading":"","excerpt":"[[../batch03/58-df-bounded-operator.md]]","embed":false},{"target":"../batch15/58-df-self-adjoint.md","status":"resolved","id":"5998e080b5d378a0","anchor":"ref-4","targetAnchor":"","location":"元数据 · depends_on","heading":"","excerpt":"[[../batch15/58-df-self-adjoint.md]]","embed":false}],"math":[{"tex":"H,T,\\langle\\cdot,\\cdot\\rangle\\in V","display":false},{"tex":"\\mathbb K\\in\\{\\mathbb R,\\mathbb C\\}","display":false},{"tex":"T\\in H^H","display":false},{"tex":"\\mathrm{HilbertSpace}_S:V^2\\to\\{\\top,\\bot\\}","display":false},{"tex":"\\mathrm{Linear}_{\\mathbb K}(-;H,H)","display":false},{"tex":"\\mathrm{BoundedOperator}_S:V^3\\to\\{\\top,\\bot\\}","display":false},{"tex":"\\operatorname{SelfAdjoint}_S:V^2\\to\\{\\top,\\bot\\}","display":false},{"tex":"\\begin{aligned}\n\\mathrm{thm\\text{-}hellinger}\\vdash&\n\\mathrm{HilbertSpace}_S(H,\\langle\\cdot,\\cdot\\rangle)\n\\land T\\in H^H\n\\land\\mathrm{Linear}_{\\mathbb K}(T;H,H)\\\\\n&\\land\n\\forall x,y\\in H\\;\n\\bigl(\n\\langle T(x),y\\rangle=\\langle x,T(y)\\rangle\n\\bigr)\\\\\n&\\to\n\\mathrm{BoundedOperator}_S(T,H,H)\n\\land\\operatorname{SelfAdjoint}_S(T,H).\n\\end{aligned}","display":true}],"bytes":1456,"backlinks":[{"id":"84daad544872cc71","anchor":"ref-4203","locations":["正文"],"count":1,"excerpt":"[[../batch08/58-thm-hellinger.md|58-thm-hellinger]]（batch08）"}],"outgoing":["b70ce791d5b1a19b","9fa59a08139e4466","2ad9c248fe18df37","5998e080b5d378a0"]}